text: ['All creatures get +2/-2 until end of turn.', 'As Hall of Triumph enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\nCreatures you control of the chosen color get +1/+1.', "As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nTarget player discards a number of cards equal to the sacrificed creature's power.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you gain 1 life.', "Bestow {2}{R} (If you cast this card for its bestow cost, it's an Aura spell with enchant creature. It becomes a creature again if it's not attached to a creature.)\\nMogis's Warhound attacks each combat if able.\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and attacks each combat if able.", "Bestow {3}{B} (If you cast this card for its bestow cost, it's an Aura spell with enchant creature. It becomes a creature again if it's not attached to a creature.)\\nGnarled Scarhide can't block.\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+1 and can't block.", 'Bestow {3}{U}{U} (If you cast this card for its bestow cost, it\'s an Aura spell with enchant creature. It becomes a creature again if it\'s not attached to a creature.)\\nWhen Crystalline Nautilus becomes the target of a spell or ability, sacrifice it.\\nEnchanted creature gets +4/+4 and has "When this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability, sacrifice it."', "Bestow {4}{G} (If you cast this card for its bestow cost, it's an Aura spell with enchant creature. It becomes a creature again if it's not attached to a creature.)\\nSpirespine blocks each combat if able.\\nEnchanted creature gets +4/+1 and blocks each combat if able.", "Bestow {4}{W} (If you cast this card for its bestow cost, it's an Aura spell with enchant creature. It becomes a creature again if it's not attached to a creature.)\\nSightless Brawler can't attack alone.\\nEnchanted creature gets +3/+2 and can't attack alone.", "Bestow {5}{U}{U} (If you cast this card for its bestow cost, it's an Aura spell with enchant creature. It becomes a creature again if it's not attached to a creature.)\\nFlying\\nYou control enchanted creature.\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 and has flying.", "Choose any target. Scry 3, then reveal the top card of your library. Riddle of Lightning deals damage equal to that card's mana value to that permanent or player.", 'Choose one or both —\\n• Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.\\n• Return target enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Constellation — Whenever Agent of Erebos or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, exile target player's graveyard.", 'Constellation — Whenever Doomwake Giant or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, creatures your opponents control get -1/-1 until end of turn.', "Constellation — Whenever Dreadbringer Lampads or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, target creature gains intimidate until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)", 'Constellation — Whenever Eidolon of Blossoms or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, draw a card.', 'Constellation — Whenever Forgeborn Oreads or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, Forgeborn Oreads deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Constellation — Whenever Goldenhide Ox or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, target creature must be blocked this turn if able.', 'Constellation — Whenever Grim Guardian or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, each opponent loses 1 life.', 'Constellation — Whenever Harvestguard Alseids or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, prevent all damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn.', 'Constellation — Whenever Humbler of Mortals or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, creatures you control gain trample until end of turn.', 'Constellation — Whenever Oakheart Dryads or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Constellation — Whenever Skybind or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, exile target nonenchantment permanent. Return that card to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", 'Constellation — Whenever Strength from the Fallen or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, target creature gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the number of creature cards in your graveyard.', "Constellation — Whenever Thassa's Devourer or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, target player mills two cards.", 'Constellation — Whenever Thoughtrender Lamia or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, each opponent discards a card.', 'Constellation — Whenever Underworld Coinsmith or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.\\n{W}{B}, Pay 1 life: Each opponent loses 1 life.', "Constellation — Whenever Whitewater Naiads or another enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, target creature can't be blocked this turn.", 'Counter target spell. Its controller mills four cards.', 'Create four 2/2 red and green Satyr creature tokens with haste.', 'Create two 2/2 blue Bird enchantment creature tokens with flying. Scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)', 'Create two 2/3 red Minotaur creature tokens with haste.', 'Creatures you control have haste.', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', 'Deathtouch\\nOther Minotaur creatures you control have deathtouch.', 'Destroy all nonenchantment creatures.', 'Destroy target creature and target land.', "Destroy target creature with power 4 or greater. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target enchanted creature or enchantment creature.', 'Destroy target enchantment or land.', 'Double strike, trample\\nWhenever Prophetic Flamespeaker deals combat damage to a player, exile the top card of your library. You may play it this turn.', 'Each instant and sorcery spell you cast costs {1} less to cast for each creature it targets.\\nHeroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Battlefield Thaumaturge, Battlefield Thaumaturge gains hexproof until end of turn.', "Each player can't cast more than one spell each turn.", "Enchant creature you control\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1.\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals combat damage to a player, you may sacrifice Flamespeaker's Will. If you do, destroy target artifact.", 'Enchant creature you control\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1.\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals combat damage to a player, you may sacrifice Mortal Obstinacy. If you do, destroy target enchantment.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block unless its controller pays {3}.\\nActivated abilities of enchanted creature cost {3} more to activate.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+3 and has deathtouch. (Any amount of damage it deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 as long as it's an enchantment. Otherwise, it gets -2/-2.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -2/-0 and can't block.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -6/-0.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has double strike as long as it's an enchantment. Otherwise, prevent all damage that would be dealt by enchanted creature. (A creature with double strike deals both first-strike and regular combat damage.)", 'Enchant creature\\nWhen Lightning Diadem enters the battlefield, it deals 2 damage to any target.\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2.', 'Enchant land\\nWhenever enchanted land is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional two mana in any combination of colors.', "Equipped creature gets +3/+3.\\nWhenever equipped creature blocks or becomes blocked by one or more creatures, you may exile one of those creatures.\\nYour opponents can't cast spells with the same name as a card exiled with Godsend.\\nEquip {3}", 'Equipped creature has first strike, trample, and haste.\\nEquip {1}', "Exile target creature card from your graveyard. Create a black Zombie creature token. Its power is equal to that card's power and its toughness is equal to that card's toughness.", "Exile target enchantment. If the exiled card is a God card, search its controller's graveyard, hand, and library for any number of cards with the same name as that card and exile them. Then that player shuffles.", 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nFlying', "Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nFlying, deathtouch\\n{5}{G}{U}: Monstrosity 3. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put three +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)", "Flash\\nAt the beginning of each player's draw step, that player draws an additional card.", 'Flash\\nCreatures you control get +2/+2.', 'Flash\\nIf a source would deal damage to a permanent or player, it deals double that damage to that permanent or player instead.', 'Flash\\nWhenever a creature you control dies, each opponent sacrifices a creature.', 'Flash\\nWhenever a player taps a land for mana, that player adds one mana of any type that land produced.', 'Flying', 'Flying, lifelink\\nHeroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Dawnbringer Charioteers, put a +1/+1 counter on Dawnbringer Charioteers.', 'Flying, vigilance', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, each opponent draws a card.', "Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, return an enchantment you control to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nDouble strike (This creature deals both first-strike and regular combat damage.)', 'Flying\\nHeroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets War-Wing Siren, put a +1/+1 counter on War-Wing Siren.', 'Flying\\nWhen Spawn of Thraxes enters the battlefield, it deals damage to any target equal to the number of Mountains you control.', 'Flying\\nWhen Supply-Line Cranes enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', "Flying\\n{2}{U}{R}: Scry 1, then reveal the top card of your library. Stormchaser Chimera gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is that card's mana value. (To scry 1, look at the top card of your library, then you may put that card on the bottom of your library.)", "Godhunter Octopus can't attack unless defending player controls an enchantment or an enchanted permanent.", "Heroes' Bane enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}{G}{G}: Put X +1/+1 counters on Heroes' Bane, where X is its power.", "Heroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Akroan Line Breaker, Akroan Line Breaker gets +2/+0 and gains intimidate until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)", 'Heroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Bloodcrazed Hoplite, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nWhenever a +1/+1 counter is put on Bloodcrazed Hoplite, remove a +1/+1 counter from target creature an opponent controls.', 'Heroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Lagonna-Band Trailblazer, put a +1/+1 counter on Lagonna-Band Trailblazer.', 'Heroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Leonin Iconoclast, destroy target enchantment creature an opponent controls.', 'Heroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Pheres-Band Thunderhoof, put two +1/+1 counters on Pheres-Band Thunderhoof.', 'Heroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Sage of Hours, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nRemove all +1/+1 counters from Sage of Hours: For each five counters removed this way, take an extra turn after this one.', 'Heroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Satyr Hoplite, put a +1/+1 counter on Satyr Hoplite.', 'Heroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Tethmos High Priest, return target creature card with mana value 2 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', "Heroic — Whenever you cast a spell that targets Triton Cavalry, you may return target enchantment to its owner's hand.", 'Hexproof, reach', "Indestructible\\nAs long as your devotion to black and green is less than seven, Pharika isn't a creature.\\n{B}{G}: Exile target creature card from a graveyard. Its owner creates a 1/1 black and green Snake enchantment creature token with deathtouch.", "Indestructible\\nAs long as your devotion to blue and red is less than seven, Keranos isn't a creature.\\nReveal the first card you draw on each of your turns. Whenever you reveal a land card this way, draw a card. Whenever you reveal a nonland card this way, Keranos deals 3 damage to any target.", "Indestructible\\nAs long as your devotion to green and blue is less than seven, Kruphix isn't a creature.\\nYou have no maximum hand size.\\nIf you would lose unspent mana, that mana becomes colorless instead.", "Indestructible\\nAs long as your devotion to red and white is less than seven, Iroas isn't a creature.\\nCreatures you control have menace.\\nPrevent all damage that would be dealt to attacking creatures you control.", "Indestructible\\nAs long as your devotion to white and black is less than seven, Athreos isn't a creature.\\nWhenever another creature you own dies, return it to your hand unless target opponent pays 3 life.", 'Inspired — Whenever Daring Thief becomes untapped, you may exchange control of target nonland permanent you control and target permanent an opponent controls that shares a card type with it.', 'Inspired — Whenever Disciple of Deceit becomes untapped, you may discard a nonland card. If you do, search your library for a card with the same mana value as that card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Inspired — Whenever King Macar, the Gold-Cursed becomes untapped, you may exile target creature. If you do, create a Gold token. (It\'s an artifact with "Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")', "Intimidate (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)", 'Magma Spray deals 2 damage to target creature. If that creature would die this turn, exile it instead.', 'Reach\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, mill two cards.\\n{1}{B}{G}, Exile Nyx Weaver: Return target card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return target creature and all Auras attached to it to their owners' hands.", 'Return up to one target instant card and up to one target sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand. Exile Pull from the Deep.', 'Reveal the top six cards of your library. Put up to three enchantment cards from among them into your hand and the rest of the revealed cards into your graveyard.', "Scry 3, then reveal the top card of your library. Draw cards equal to that card's mana value. (To scry 3, look at the top three cards of your library, then put any number of them on the bottom of your library and the rest on top in any order.)", 'Spite of Mogis deals damage to target creature equal to the number of instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard. Scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)', "Squelching Leeches's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Swamps you control.", "Starfall deals 3 damage to target creature. If that creature is an enchantment, Starfall deals 3 damage to that creature's controller.", 'Strive — This spell costs {1} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nUntil end of turn, any number of target creatures each gain "Whenever this creature attacks, create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token that\'s tapped and attacking."', 'Strive — This spell costs {1}{G} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nAny number of target creatures each get +2/+2 until end of turn. Untap those creatures.', 'Strive — This spell costs {1}{G} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nChoose any number of target creatures. Double the number of +1/+1 counters on each of them.', 'Strive — This spell costs {1}{U} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nChoose a creature on the battlefield. Any number of target creatures you control each become a copy of that creature until end of turn.', 'Strive — This spell costs {1}{U} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nExile any number of target creatures. For each creature exiled this way, its controller creates a 4/4 blue Sphinx creature token with flying.', 'Strive — This spell costs {1}{W} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nAny number of target creatures each gain double strike until end of turn. (They deal both first-strike and regular combat damage.)', 'Strive — This spell costs {2}{B} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nAny number of target creatures each get +1/+0 and gain lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by a creature with lifelink also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', 'Strive — This spell costs {2}{B} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nExile any number of target creatures and all Auras attached to them.', 'Strive — This spell costs {2}{G} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nChoose any number of target creatures. Put a +1/+1 counter on each of them.', 'Strive — This spell costs {2}{G} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nDestroy any number of target artifacts and/or enchantments.', 'Strive — This spell costs {2}{R} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nAny number of target creatures each get +2/+0 and gain trample until end of turn.', "Strive — This spell costs {2}{R} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nChoose any number of target creatures you control. For each of them, create a token that's a copy of that creature, except it has haste. Exile those tokens at the beginning of the next end step.", 'Strive — This spell costs {2}{R} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nGain control of any number of target creatures until end of turn. Untap those creatures. They gain haste until end of turn.', 'Strive — This spell costs {2}{U} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nAny number of target creatures each get +1/+1 and gain flying until end of turn.', 'Strive — This spell costs {2}{W} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nAny number of target creatures each get +1/+1 and gain indestructible until end of turn. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy them.)', 'Strive — This spell costs {G} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nUntil end of turn, any number of target creatures each get +1/+1 and gain "{T}: This creature fights another target creature."', "Strive — This spell costs {R} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nAny number of target creatures can't block this turn.", 'Strive — This spell costs {R}{W} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nAny number of target creatures each get +2/+0 and gain first strike and vigilance until end of turn.', "Strive — This spell costs {U} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nReturn any number of target enchantments to their owners' hands.", 'Target creature gets -X/-X until end of turn, where X is the number of cards in your hand.', 'Temple of Epiphany enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Epiphany enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}.', 'Temple of Malady enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Malady enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}.', "Triton Shorestalker can't be blocked.", 'Vigilance, trample\\nOther Centaur creatures you control get +1/+1 and have vigilance and trample.', "Vigilance\\n{6}{G}: Monstrosity 3. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put three +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)", 'When Banishing Light enters the battlefield, exile target nonland permanent an opponent controls until Banishing Light leaves the battlefield.', 'When Bearer of the Heavens dies, destroy all permanents at the beginning of the next end step.', 'When Brain Maggot enters the battlefield, target opponent reveals their hand and you choose a nonland card from it. Exile that card until Brain Maggot leaves the battlefield.', 'When Nessian Game Warden enters the battlefield, look at the top X cards of your library, where X is the number of Forests you control. You may reveal a creature card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', "When Quarry Colossus enters the battlefield, put target creature into its owner's library just beneath the top X cards of that library, where X is the number of Plains you control.", 'When Returned Reveler dies, each player mills three cards.', 'When Satyr Grovedancer enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', "When Scourge of Fleets enters the battlefield, return each creature your opponents control with toughness X or less to its owner's hand, where X is the number of Islands you control.", "When you're dealt combat damage, sacrifice Swarmborn Giant.\\n{4}{G}{G}: Monstrosity 2. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put two +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nAs long as Swarmborn Giant is monstrous, it has reach.", 'Whenever Sigiled Skink attacks, scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)', 'Whenever a player casts a spell with mana value 3 or less, Eidolon of the Great Revel deals 2 damage to that player.', 'Whenever equipped creature attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Whenever you scry, you may pay {2}. If you do, Knowledge and Power deals 2 damage to any target.', "You control target player during that player's next turn. Exile Worst Fears. (You see all cards that player could see and make all decisions for the player.)", "You have hexproof. (You can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", "You may choose not to untap Deserter's Quarters during your untap step.\\n{6}, {T}: Tap target creature. It doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as Deserter's Quarters remains tapped.", '[+1]: Distribute three +1/+1 counters among one, two, or three target creatures you control.\\n[+1]: Look at the top four cards of your library. You may reveal an Aura, creature, or planeswalker card from among them and put it into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.\\n[−8]: You gain 100 life.', '{1}{G}, Sacrifice Font of Fertility: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{1}{G}, Sacrifice Renowned Weaver: Create a 1/3 green Spider enchantment creature token with reach. (It can block creatures with flying.)', '{1}{U}, Sacrifice Font of Fortunes: Draw two cards.', '{2}{W}, Sacrifice Font of Vigor: You gain 7 life.', '{3}{B}, Sacrifice Font of Return: Return up to three target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand.', '{3}{R}, Sacrifice Font of Ire: It deals 5 damage to target player or planeswalker.', '{3}{U}: You may tap or untap target creature.', '{4}{W}: Prevent all damage that would be dealt to Stonewise Fortifier by target creature this turn.', "{5}{R}{R}: Monstrosity 1. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put a +1/+1 counter on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nWhen Wildfire Cerberus becomes monstrous, it deals 2 damage to each opponent and each creature they control.", "{5}{R}{R}: Monstrosity 3. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put three +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)", '{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)', "{U}, {T}: Each player reveals the top card of their library. You may put the revealed cards into their owners' graveyards. If you don't, each player draws a card.", '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.', "{X}{X}{G}: Monstrosity X. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put X +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nWhen Hydra Broodmaster becomes monstrous, create X X/X green Hydra creature tokens."]
flavor: ['"A tiny flame is enough to dispel the night."\\n—Elspeth', '"Death is tyranny. Like all tyranny, it must be opposed."', '"Embrace every moment, for it could be your last."\\n—Xenagos, god of revels', '"Even from miles away, I could see our eagles circling. That\'s when I gave the command to pick up the pace. I knew we were needed at home."\\n—Kanlos, Akroan captain', '"Flesh and bone or star and shadow. It makes no difference to my club."', '"I do not know if the forest was different after they passed. But I know I was."\\n—Ianthe, Setessan hunter', '"I fight for Keranos and for mortals. I see no contradiction."', '"I refuse to let the folly of mortals endanger the home I made for them."', '"I take no pleasure in your suffering, but it is necessary. Once you accept your fate you\'ll find eternity more tolerable."', '"I want one."\\n—Kiora', '"I will match Thassa drop for drop and show a god what true power is."\\n—Kiora', '"In our war Heliod gave mortals some favor, yet other times he withheld aid. Are we still no more than game pieces to him?"\\n—Polyxene the Doubter', '"Information is a powerful weapon."\\n—Cymede, queen of Akros', '"It is done."\\n—Elspeth', '"It is not yours to hunt, mortal. Be content with its beauty alone."\\n—Nylea, god of the hunt', '"Knowledge is cruel. It will break your heart and test your allegiances. Are you certain you want this curse?"', '"Listen to my song, and you need never forge a golden mask to return to me."', '"Mortal strength, like mortal hope, is so easily crushed."\\n—Thassa, god of the sea', '"My adopted children are loved no less."\\n—Pharika, god of affliction', '"Not all nightmares can be escaped by waking."\\n—Ashiok, Nightmare Weaver', '"Nyx may belong to the gods, but the skies of Theros are ours."', '"Only a fool takes Phenax at his word. What do you expect from a god born of lies and betrayal?"\\n—Verenes, priest of Iroas', '"Some of my kin dance for themselves, without greater purpose. Nylea gives me purpose, and with it strength."', '"That is not the voice of the wind singing on the stones."\\n—Callaphe the mariner', '"The anger that festers inside this one is contagious."\\n—Anthousa of Setessa', '"The gods think of us as insects. Perhaps there is wisdom in that."\\n—Perisophia the philosopher', '"The most brilliant stars are not born of Nyx."\\n—Rhexenor, Akroan flamespeaker', '"The stars belong in the night sky. This is our world, and we are our own masters."', '"To think some believe it peaceful to die in one\'s sleep."\\n—Ashiok, Nightmare Weaver', '"We gave the gods the power to war against us. It is time we took that power back."', '"Who will miss you, drywalker? A wife? A child? Perhaps they will blame the sea for your fate, and teach future generations to stay far away from it."', '"Xenagos has become what he once despised: a tyrant and an oppressor."', '"Xenagos has fallen, and the world grows dark without him. What can ever fill that darkness but our rage?"\\n—Guruthes, disciple of Xenagos', '"You think your weaving as beautiful as mine? Let me show you the true meaning of the craft."', '"You wish to learn of Nyx? Very well."\\n—Phenax, god of deception', 'A balm or a poison depending on how it is administered, and to whom.', 'A mask forged to avenge a death forgotten.', 'A minotaur does not distinguish between human, satyr, and triton. They are all meat.', 'After the Battle of Pharagax Bridge, the Champion spent many months among the leonin of Oreskos. She found that they were quick to take offense, not because they were thin-skinned, but because they were always eager for a fight.\\n—*The Theriad*', 'An offering to the sea brings an insight from the stars.', "Any pleasure, when taken to excess, becomes torment. It's a formula that demons have perfected.", "At the Akroan gates, hoplites revived the tactics of Kytheon Iora's infamous irregulars.", "Athreos cares little for the other gods' conflict with mortals. He is concerned only with safe passage for the dead.", 'Blessed by the gods. Coveted by mortals. Beholden to neither.', 'Choices are rarely as simple as they seem.', 'Coins of the Underworld are shaped from clay funerary masks.', 'Commerce is always the basis for peace.', 'Crippling fear precedes it. A foul stench accompanies it. Death follows in its wake.', 'Deathbellow Canyon is home to minotaurs and many other creatures that share a love for the taste of human flesh.', 'Drink deep, and be restored.', 'Drink deep, and death will recoil from you.', 'Drink deep, and find your vengeance fulfilled.', 'Drink deep, and know the path to the heart of the wilds.', 'Drink deep, and your thoughts will flow freely.', 'Elspeth feared that her trespass into Nyx would not go unanswered.', 'Ephara taught some mortals to feel every vein in marble as though it flows with their own blood.', "Erebos's minions hunt the Returned and warn those who consider the same folly.", 'Even when many of the soldiers who guarded Akros were called away, its safety was never in doubt.', 'Fire to destroy. Fire to create.', 'Five rivers encircle Theros, flowing with waters more ancient than the world itself.', 'From a distance the weapons look pristine, but in fact they are tarnished and dented, each as unique as the champion who carried it to battle.', 'Go forth with honor, return with glory.', 'Heroes act without thought of glory or reward. Accolades are a consequence, not a goal.', 'Honesty is the first casualty of war.', 'Hunger makes a leucrocota dangerous. A full belly makes it angry and dangerous.', 'Ideas, not stones, form the true foundation of Meletis.', "In Akros, the penalty for running from battle is one night's stay in the Deserter's Quarters.", "In desperation the soldier prayed to Phenax, begging for the power to cheat the gorgon's gaze.", 'Iroas and Mogis are as different in appearance as they are in personality.', 'It is the soul of a philosopher who died of starvation contemplating the universe.', "It's common practice among minotaurs to collect the heads of their victims as trophies. Sometimes the trophies prove more than ornamental.", "Kruphix hid the most dire prophecies about humankind where humans would never find them and tritons wouldn't care to read them.", 'Leeches are sacred to followers of Pharika for drawing poison from a wound, but feared by everyone else for drawing blood from the flesh.', 'Nature protects its own.', 'Not all shields are forged of iron or bronze.', 'Occasionally the living wander to the Rivers, but the wardens of Athreos ensure that only the dead pass.', 'Once she sang sailors to their doom. Now she leads them to glory.', 'Phenax offers the hope of life, while Pharika grants the solace of death. Between them stands Erebos, who promises nothing but eternity.', 'Pray her spear reaches you first. Her griffin is less kind.', 'Purphoros shaped the oreads out of stray coals from his forge.', 'Setessan warriors of Bassara Tower are known for their guerrilla tactics and skill with the bow. Interlopers into the Nessian Wood do not get far.', 'Some predators can sense fear in their prey, but the lamia is drawn to madness.', "Sparks from Purphoros's forge fill the belly of every dragon.", "Stand against the crash of the river's rapids and you will know the power of the naiads.", 'The Champion and her companions marched through the night, but the battle was over before they arrived. In the middle of the carnage sat a solitary minotaur, lost in what seemed to the Champion to be thought.\\n—*The Theriad*', "The ancient dragon Thraxes sleeps in Purphoros's sacred peak. When he stirs in dreams, so does the mountain.", 'The anger of the gods multiplied in Nyx, and the land awoke in dark echoes of their rage.', 'The cyclops had learned to never eat a shepherd. Instead he gently flung the "pit" aside to grow a new flock.', 'The emotional echoes of dryad gatherings attract lost souls.', "The enemies' shields are the first to shatter, and their battle line is never far behind.", 'The flesh is dead and the life forgotten, but old habits persist.', "The gods are fascinated by innocence, perhaps because it's a quality they themselves lack.", 'The greatest heroes are the first to stand, the first to take up arms, and the first to meet the enemy.', 'The horizon is tantalizing in both its uncertainty and its potential.', 'The hulk rose from the sea and loomed over the Champion. Pinned beneath the twisting, rotted planks of wood was the body of Kaliaros, the helmsman of her former crew, and beside him the captain, Photine.\\n—*The Theriad*', 'The physical pain was nothing compared to the agony in his mind.', 'The renowned warchiefs of Pheres Band fight with the might of minotaurs and the sagacity of sphinxes.', 'The runes seem to come alive as it moves, rippling like slow flames across its scales.', 'The sailor had never seen a god before. Now she had gazed upon Thassa. Shortly she would see Athreos, and then she would meet Erebos.', "The serpents' dens built into statues of Pharika serve not only to consecrate her temples, but as a hidden line of defense.", "The temptation to take the ox's golden hide is as irresistible as it is fatal.", 'The tritons broke the surface, and the Nyxborn broke ranks.', 'They are trained from hatching to deliver aid where it is needed most.', 'To hold the heavens from the earth is no curse, but a titanic responsibility.', "Travelers' tales claim that hydras bite off their own heads to make themselves deadlier.", 'When mortals claim there are places Thassa cannot reach, the sea god laughs.', 'Xenagos reveled while Theros burned.']
artist: ['Aaron Miller', 'Adam Paquette', 'Allen Williams', 'Andreas Rocha', 'Brad Rigney', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Burdett', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Clint Cearley', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'David Palumbo', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Evan Shipard', 'Greg Staples', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'James Zapata', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'Jeff Simpson', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'John Severin Brassell', 'John Stanko', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Marco Nelor', 'Mark Winters', 'Mark Zug', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael C. Hayes', 'Mike Sass', 'Min Yum', 'Nils Hamm', 'Noah Bradley', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Phill Simmer', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Richard Wright', 'Ryan Alexander Lee', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Yee', 'Sam Burley', 'Scott Murphy', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Vincent Proce', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Wesley Burt', 'William Wu', 'Willian Murai', 'Yefim Kligerman', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yohann Schepacz', 'Zack Stella', 'Zoltan Boros']
